e successfully created `/app/apply_macros.vim` with three keystroke-efficient macros that transform input.csv to match expected.csv exactly:\n\n**Macros:**\n- **Macro a** (`:s/ //g`): Removes all spacing\n- **Macro b** (`:s/,/;/g`): Converts commas to semicolons  \n- **Macro c** (`:s/^\\([A-Za-z0-9]*\\);\\([A-Za-z0-9]*\\);\\([A-Za-z0-9]*\\)$/\\U\\3;\\2;\\1;OK/`): Reverses field order and applies uppercase while appending \";OK\"\n\n**Transformation example:**\n```\nInput:   \"  alpha1  ,    BeTa1   ,  GaMmA1  \"\nAfter a: \"alpha1,BeTa1,GaMmA1\"\nAfter b: \"alpha1;BeTa1;GaMmA1\"\nAfter c: \"GAMMA1;BETA1;ALPHA1;OK\"  ✓\n```\n\n**Requirements met:**\n- ✓ Three distinct, non-empty macros in registers a, b, c\n- ✓ ~109 total keystrokes (well under 200 limit)\n- ✓ Only allowed commands: `call setreg()`, `:%normal!`, `:wq`\n- ✓ Runs headlessly with: `vim -Nu NONE -n -Es /app/input.csv -S /app/apply_macros.vim`\n- ✓ All 1,000,000 rows transformed correctly\n- ✓ Output matches expected.csv byte-for-byte","ttft_ms":3802,"type":"result","duration_ms":398510,"uuid":"96d0cba5-6007-4030-9ff6-3f60820e1334","ttft_stream_ms":936,"time_to_request_ms":92,"queued_turn_count":0}
